From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:17:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: let the CPU cluster
 power gates apply

t8132.dtsi describes the CPU clusters' power-gate enables in
/arm-io/pmgr reg[34], E at +0x0 and P at +0x60, and
apple-cluster-pwrgate sets bit 31 of both at its early initcall, before
the secondary CPUs start. The J604 lab file redeclares that node with
status "disabled". That dates from when the layout was only known from
another board, and nothing was to be written before the words had been
read on the machine.

They have been read since: with both clusters up the J604 has
0x80000000 at +0x0 and 0 at +0x60, as on the J713, where iBoot sets the
E word only. The J604 boots on a P core, so its boot cluster enters
every deep sleep with its enable clear; only the way back from a sleep
sets it. The J713, whose deep sleeps resume, has the node enabled.

Drop the J604 redeclaration, so the J604 takes t8132.dtsi's node as the
J713 does.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 9 ---------
 1 file changed, 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 594b92e09a..c88e1373d4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -257,15 +257,6 @@ cpu_ctrl: cpu-ctrl@380734000 {
 		reg-names = "cpu-start", "acc0", "acc1";
 		apple,pmgr = <&pmgr>;
 	};
-	/*
-	 * The CPU clusters' power-gate enables, in /arm-io/pmgr reg[34]:
-	 * cluster 0 (E) at +0x0, cluster 1 (P) at +0x60. iBoot sets E's only.
-	 */
-	cluster_pwrgate: power-gate@380724000 {
-		compatible = "apple,t8132-cluster-pwrgate", "apple,cluster-pwrgate";
-		reg = <0x03 0x80724000 0x00 0x04>, <0x03 0x80724060 0x00 0x04>;
-		status = "disabled";
-	};
 	pmgr_sleep: power-management@3882c8000 {
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-pmgr-sleep";
 		reg = <0x03 0x882c8000 0x00 0x1000>, <0x03 0x88004000 0x00 0x60>, <0x03 0x80760000 0x00 0x530>;
-- 
